 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "Always state the **assumptions**: all workers or pumps work at the same rate, the job is fixed, and the food is eaten at the same rate. Without them the proportion may not hold."),
 ("h2", "Working Together"),
 ("p", "Treat the whole job as **1 unit of work**. If A finishes it in 2 hours and B in 3 hours, then in one hour A does 1/2 and B does 1/3, so together they do 1/2 + 1/3 = **5/6** of the work per hour. Time for the whole job = 1 ÷ 5/6 = **6/5 hours = 1 h 12 min**."),
 ("note", "REMEMBER", "Add the **rates** (work per hour), not the times. Two pumps that fill a tank in 3 h and 2 h do **not** take 5 hours together; together they take less than the faster pump alone."),
